diff --git a/CHANGES/v2.10.md b/CHANGES/v2.10.md
index 9125722a69..78d6a4d29f 100644
--- a/CHANGES/v2.10.md
+++ b/CHANGES/v2.10.md
@@ -102,3 +102,14 @@ Before switching to version 2.10, users are invited to carefully read the follow
     OPES multithermal and the well-tempered ensemble crash on more than one MPI rank.
   - Documentation: ENERGY does include the GROMACS long tail (`DispCorr`) corrections, contrary
     to what the manual stated. See [issue 567](https://github.com/plumed/plumed2/issues/567).
+  - Fixed the GROMACS 2025 and 2026 patches so that PLUMED is told before the force calculation
+    that GROMACS writes a checkpoint, as with the GROMACS 2024 patch. Actions that write their
+    state on checkpoints, such as [OPES_METAD](OPES_METAD.md) with STATE_WFILE and no STATE_WSTRIDE,
+    wrote it one step after each GROMACS checkpoint, and never at the last step. With more than one
+    MPI rank per simulation, only the main rank wrote it, and the run deadlocked at the first checkpoint.
+    See [#1430](https://github.com/plumed/plumed2/pull/1430).
+  - Fixed `-replex` together with `-plumed` in the GROMACS 2025 and 2026 patches: with GROMACS in mixed
+    precision, mdrun stopped at the first step because the bias was read into a double.
+  - Fixed the GROMACS 2025 patch so that `-multidir` simulations without `-plumed` do not have to run
+    in lockstep, which made them deadlock when they had different numbers of steps. As in the
+    GROMACS 2026 patch, the multi-simulation record is now used only when PLUMED is active.
